<graph edgedefault="undirected"><node id="AUTHOR">
  <data key="d0">AUTHOR</data>
  <data key="d1">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d2">The author of the book 'An Unsentimental Journey Through Cornwall.' The author is known for writing 'John Halifax, Gentleman.' The author emphasizes a thoughtful and immersive approach to travel, advocating for a slower, more reflective way of experiencing places rather than rushing through them. The author also mentions being called 'the old hen' due to their habit of guiding others on journeys. This entity is central to the narrative and provides the perspective through which the journey is described.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6196f7575ff952a3f5db2b2d296af03f</data>
  <data key="d4">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 23}]</data>
</node>
<node id="AN UNSENTIMENTAL JOURNEY THROUGH CORNWALL">
  <data key="d0">AN UNSENTIMENTAL JOURNEY THROUGH CORNWALL</data>
  <data key="d1">BOOK</data>
  <data key="d2">A book written by the author of 'John Halifax, Gentleman.' It is titled 'An Unsentimental Journey Through Cornwall' and serves as the primary subject of the text. The book outlines the author's philosophy on travel and includes descriptions of various locations in Cornwall. The book is significant as it frames the entire narrative and conveys the author's views on travel and observation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6196f7575ff952a3f5db2b2d296af03f</data>
  <data key="d4">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 24}]</data>
</node>
<node id="ST. MICHAEL'S MOUNT">
  <data key="d0">ST. MICHAEL'S MOUNT</data>
  <data key="d1">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d2">A location in Cornwall, England. It is mentioned in the text as one of the places that will be visited during the journey. St. Michael's Mount is a notable landmark, often associated with historical and cultural significance. The text references it as part of the journey, indicating its importance in the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;A location in Cornwall, known for its historical and legendary associations. It is described as a rocky island with a castle, and it is linked to many legends involving figures like Cormoran and Jack.&lt;SEP&gt;A location that is a rocky hill with a fortress at the top, surrounded by the sea. It is described as a place with a mix of medieval and modern elements, including a fishing village at the base and a small underground railway. Its significance lies in its historical and architectural value, as well as its unique position in the landscape. It is connected to the St. Aubyns and the event involving one of their daughters falling from the battlements.&lt;SEP&gt;St. Michael's Mount is a tidal island in Cornwall, England, famous for its castle and historical significance. It is described as shining in the setting sun and is the destination of the royal visit. This location is important as it is the site of the royal party's arrival and is central to the narrative of the story.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3d113b2b3dce6fe310bc06ea08b364cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-744360fec46b02217eb1d4d9f455cb8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-369d72e297f786886a6ee02d55512e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6196f7575ff952a3f5db2b2d296af03f</data>
  <data key="d4">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}]</data>
</node>
<node id="FALMOUTH">
  <data key="d0">FALMOUTH</data>
  <data key="d1">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d2">A location in Cornwall, England, where the travelers begin their journey. It is described as having a sheltered bay and glittering sea. Falmouth is significant as it is the starting point of the journey and is contrasted with the more rustic Green Bank. It is also mentioned as a place where the travelers meet their friend who helps them with arrangements.&lt;SEP&gt;A location in Cornwall, England. Falmouth is mentioned in the text as a place that will be explored. It is a coastal town known for its harbor and maritime history. The text references Falmouth as part of the journey, highlighting its role in the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;A location in Cornwall, mentioned as a possible destination for picnics and tourist activities. It is contrasted with the more secluded and romantic aspects of Kynance Sands.&lt;SEP&gt;A location that is part of the group's travel route. It is described as having a 'good road,' but also as 'rather lonely.' The group considers it as part of their journey and it plays a role in their decision to return to civilization.&lt;SEP&gt;Falmouth is a coastal town in Cornwall, England, known for its harbor and scenic views. It is mentioned as a destination in the journey, and the Green Bank Hotel is referenced as an alternative to the more modern Falmouth Hotel. Falmouth is significant as a location where the travelers choose to stay.&lt;SEP&gt;Falmouth is a location mentioned in the text, likely a town or city. It is referenced as a destination where Charles is expected to return. The name suggests it is a significant settlement, possibly a port or a commercial center. It plays a role in the travel plans of the ladies and Charles.&lt;SEP&gt;Falmouth is a town in Cornwall, mentioned as a destination in the journey. It serves as a reference point for the route taken by the travelers. Falmouth is significant in the context of the narrative as it represents a key location in the region.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c527f463c6b54a8cb919a64d12423b24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6196f7575ff952a3f5db2b2d296af03f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85b0c1bb6db9932af72e242802e01101&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fb3571cbea81efe6dfda2aa2199fdbe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ee024234b415f45ea0006087720bb09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-743cd293533b6212903371567d44500f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f15d171fef48d074f3c095117c010dc</data>
