<node id="KYNANCE COVE">
  <data key="d0">KYNANCE COVE</data>
  <data key="d1">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d2">A location in Cornwall, England. Kynance Cove is mentioned in the text as a destination during the journey. It is a picturesque cove known for its natural beauty and rock formations. The text references the Steeple Rock and the Lion Rocks, indicating the significance of this location in the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;Kynance Cove is a coastal location in Cornwall, described as a place of natural beauty and significance. It is mentioned as a destination for exploration and is associated with the surrounding rocks and islands. Its importance lies in its scenic value and its role in the narrative as a place of interest and adventure.&lt;SEP&gt;Kynance Cove is a location referenced in the text, which the narrator plans to visit. It is described as a scenic spot with caves and a steep path leading to the cove. The location is central to the narrator's journey and is highlighted as a destination worth visiting.&lt;SEP&gt;Kynance Cove is a specific geographical location mentioned in the text. It is described as a beautiful place with natural features like waves, rocks, and caves. The location plays a central role in the narrative, serving as the setting for the events and interactions described. It is associated with the characters and their activities, and it evokes a sense of beauty and adventure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f0a99969e1d14b8295d2ca8754d35856&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1d2b2559cbc455b5cb2409b4efdaf8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df082bbea6d90a549cd8b56e6131733a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6196f7575ff952a3f5db2b2d296af03f</data>
  <data key="d4">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 22}]</data>
</node>
<node id="ST. IVES">
  <data key="d0">ST. IVES</data>
  <data key="d1">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d2">A coastal town in Cornwall, England, known for its pilchard fishery and historical significance. It is the setting of the narrative and is described as a small, charming town. The town's importance lies in its cultural and economic role in the region.&lt;SEP&gt;A location in Cornwall, England. St. Ives is mentioned in the text as a place that will be visited. It is a coastal town known for its artistic heritage and scenic beauty. The text references St. Ives as part of the journey, highlighting its appeal to travelers.&lt;SEP&gt;A town immortalized by a nursery rhyme about a man with seven wives. It is described as having two roads, one good and one beautiful. The significance of this location lies in its cultural reference through the nursery rhyme and its scenic beauty. It is connected to the journey taken by the narrator and is contrasted with Penzance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c07a1f8303c88520a6e687ca76451218&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-744360fec46b02217eb1d4d9f455cb8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6196f7575ff952a3f5db2b2d296af03f</data>
