<node id="ST. RUMON">
  <data key="d0">ST. RUMON</data>
  <data key="d1">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d2">St. Rumon is an Irish bishop who is said to have settled on Goonhilly Down, far from the world, and made a cell and oratory. His memory and name are still preserved by the villages of Ruan Major and Ruan Minor. He is significant for his historical and religious role in the region.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c3755e64526057a08de86199d3391703</data>
</node>
<node id="GOONHILLY DOWN">
  <data key="d0">GOONHILLY DOWN</data>
  <data key="d1">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d2">A location known for its scenic beauty and coastal features. It is described as a high plain with a sparkling sea beyond it, and it is associated with the Lizard Lights, a significant structure in the area. This place is central to the narrative, where the characters explore and experience the natural environment.&lt;SEP&gt;Goonhilly Down is a wide, treeless area in Cornwall that was once believed to be a forest full of wild beasts. It is now a flat, bare landscape known for its unique geological features and the Cornish heath. Its name comes from the old Cornish language, meaning 'hunting ground.'</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c3755e64526057a08de86199d3391703&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cff43d4c0b87d4d234e1ded07f8597b</data>
