<node id="SERPENTINE">
  <data key="d0">SERPENTINE</data>
  <data key="d1">MATERIAL</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of rock used in various crafts and constructions. The text describes the serpentine works in Poltesco, highlighting the variety of items made from this material, including mantelpieces, tombstones, and jewelry. It is a key resource in the local economy.&lt;SEP&gt;Serpentine is a type of rock found along the coast of Cornwall, particularly near Lizard Town. It is known for its reddish and greenish colors and is used in making ornaments, candlesticks, and brooches. It forms a distinct geological line in the region.</data>
