  <data key="d1">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d2">A character in the narrative who is described as being practical-minded and cautious. They are part of the group exploring the Cornish coast and are involved in the decision to go out and adventure. Their perspective adds depth to the story.&lt;SEP&gt;A person who is observing the sunset from the cliffs. They reflect on the beauty of nature and the fleeting moments of life. This individual is likely an older woman, as indicated by the reference to 'an equally harmless old woman.' Their role in the context is that of an observer and contemplator of natural beauty.&lt;SEP&gt;The narrator is an individual who observes and reflects on the events described in the text. They are part of a group that lingers after a service, admires decorations, and later travels with John Curgenven. Their perspective shapes the narrative and highlights the experiences and emotions of the characters involved.</data>
