  <data key="d1">ANIMAL</data>
  <data key="d2">The Cornish chough is a bird species native to Cornwall, mentioned in the text as a symbol of the local folklore. It is said to be the form in which King Arthur haunts the coast, linking the natural and mythical elements of the narrative. The Cornish chough is an important part of the region's wildlife and cultural identity.</data>
