<node id="LIZARD LIGHTS">
  <data key="d0">LIZARD LIGHTS</data>
  <data key="d1">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d2">A structure used to guide ships safely to shore, particularly during dark nights. The Lizard Lights are described as being as bright as 20,000 candles and visible from great distances.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of light produced by the Lizard Lights, described as being equivalent to 30,000 candles. It is a significant technological achievement that serves the purpose of guiding ships and preventing accidents.&lt;SEP&gt;The Lizard Lights are a natural phenomenon mentioned in the text, likely referring to a glowing stream or a light display. They are described as contending with the harvest moon, suggesting they are a visual spectacle. Their significance lies in their beauty and the atmosphere they create during the night. They are part of the setting of the journey and contribute to the mood of the narrative.</data>
