  <data key="d1">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d2">A person who experienced the storm in Cornwall. They describe their feelings and observations about the environment and the events that occurred during the storm. Their role is central to the narrative, as they provide first-hand accounts of the weather and its impact on their surroundings. Key attributes include their emotional response to the storm and their reflections on the experience. This entity is connected to the Lizard storm and the literary works mentioned in the text. There is no historical or cultural relevance associated with this entity beyond the narrative itself.&lt;SEP&gt;A person who is part of the group traveling in Cornwall. They are described as being content with solitude and enjoying both society and quiet moments. Their reflection on life and death suggests they are introspective and philosophical.&lt;SEP&gt;A person who is part of the narrative, likely a traveler or observer. They are described as being in a field and observing various landmarks. Their role is to provide a first-person perspective on the journey.</data>
