<node id="SENNEN">
  <data key="d0">SENNEN</data>
  <data key="d1">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d2">A location that is part of the group's travel route. It is described as having an 'ancient church' and a 'new school house.' The group passes through it and reflects on its charm and potential as a holiday resort.&lt;SEP&gt;A small village near the Land's End, known for its fishing community and proximity to Sennen. It is described as a simple, isolated community that rarely interacts with tourists. The village is associated with the fisher wife and the schoolchildren who live there. It is part of the local landscape and plays a role in the narrative of the visit.&lt;SEP&gt;Sennen is a village in Cornwall where the narrator plans to visit an afternoon church service. It is mentioned as a place they had heard about from a family acquaintance who was once a curate there. This location holds sentimental value due to the connection with the narrator's past.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a5e39286406a99236327034e4840f578&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fb3571cbea81efe6dfda2aa2199fdbe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ca4427317d91b282aad105e4c1fcb34</data>
</node>
<node id="ST. SENNEN'S">
  <data key="d0">ST. SENNEN'S</data>
  <data key="d1">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d2">St. Sennen's is a church in Sennen that the narrator had promised to visit. It is associated with the memory of a family acquaintance who served as a curate there. The church represents a link to the past and a place of spiritual significance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2ca4427317d91b282aad105e4c1fcb34</data>
</node>
<node id="ST. BURYAN'S">
  <data key="d0">ST. BURYAN'S</data>
  <data key="d1">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d2">St. Buryan's is an old church in Cornwall, noted for being founded on the site where Saint Buriana lived as a hermit. It is described as having few notable features other than the atmosphere of peace and solitude. This location reflects the religious heritage of the region.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2ca4427317d91b282aad105e4c1fcb34</data>
</node>
<node id="TRERYN">
  <data key="d0">TRERYN</data>
  <data key="d1">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d2">Treryn is a location near the famous Logan or rocking-stone. It is described as the nearest point to this natural wonder, which the narrator had read about since childhood. The area is significant for its scenic beauty and the historical event involving Lieutenant Goldsmith.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2ca4427317d91b282aad105e4c1fcb34</data>
</node>
<node id="LIEUTENANT GOLDSMITH">
  <data key="d0">LIEUTENANT GOLDSMITH</data>
  <data key="d1">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d2">Lieutenant Goldsmith is a person who attempted to move the Logan stone in 1824, causing damage to it. His actions are described as rash and foolish, leading to a legal consequence where he was forced to return the stone. This individual represents a historical figure whose actions impacted the natural landmark.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2ca4427317d91b282aad105e4c1fcb34</data>
  <data key="d4">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 25}]</data>
</node>
