<node id="CULTURAL IDENTITY OF ENGLAND">
  <data key="d3">chunk-f311566cae6280b6a50b89cb64a60d83</data>
  <data key="d2">The relationship between the legend of Arthur and the cultural identity of England is indirect, as it stems from the belief that Arthur will return to restore the Order of Knights of the Round Table. This third-order relationship has shaped the national consciousness and inspired literary works such as Tennyson's poetry. The legend of Arthur continues to influence modern interpretations of heroism and leadership.</data>
