  <data key="d2">The relationship between King Arthur and the concept of idealized heroism is direct and thematic. The text presents King Arthur as a symbol of moral virtue, love, and justice. This idealized image of Arthur influences the way the landscape and history of Cornwall are perceived, reinforcing the idea that the region is connected to a legacy of noble values and heroic deeds.</data>
