<node id="PEOPLE OF CORNWALL">
  <data key="d3">chunk-9dca5f3a8de43d3e2bc3bc88b3703f62</data>
  <data key="d2">The relationship between the landscape of Cornwall and the development of a unique cultural identity is indirect and historical. The text implies that the harsh and beautiful environment of Cornwall shaped the character of its people, making them capable of both great virtues and terrible crimes. This relationship underscores the idea that geography plays a role in shaping human behavior and cultural traditions.</data>
