<edge source="ST. IVES" target="PENZANCE">
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
  <data key="d6">The narrator compared St. Ives with Penzance, choosing the less conventional road to St. Ives. This relationship highlights the decision-making process based on aesthetic and personal preferences. The significance of this relationship is that it illustrates the contrast between different towns and the impact of choice on the travel experience. The relationship evolved as the narrator reflected on the differences between the two towns, ultimately favoring the more scenic route. The decision to take the less conventional road led to a more enjoyable and memorable journey.</data>
