  <data key="d5">1.45</data>
  <data key="d6">The inhabitant of St. Ives guides the narrator through the town, sharing information about local attractions and his personal life. This relationship is characterized by kindness and hospitality, reflecting the inhabitant's friendly nature and desire to help strangers.&lt;SEP&gt;The inhabitant's interaction with the narrator indirectly influences their perception of St. Ives. This second-order relationship shows how the inhabitant's guidance affects the narrator's experience and appreciation of the town.</data>
