  <data key="d8">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="TINTAGEL" target="KING ARTHUR">
  <data key="d5">1.75</data>
  <data key="d6">The relationship between King Arthur and Tintagel is rooted in legend and historical significance. Tintagel is believed to be a place of great importance in Arthurian lore, and it is associated with the mythical origins of King Arthur. This relationship is central to the cultural and historical identity of the region, linking the physical site to the legendary figure.&lt;SEP&gt;The relationship between Tintagel and King Arthur's grave is direct and spatial. Tintagel is a location in Cornwall where the narrator is told that King Arthur's grave is situated. This connection highlights the mythological and historical significance of Tintagel in relation to Arthurian legend. The grave's presence in the landscape reinforces the idea that the region is steeped in ancient lore and cultural memory.</data>
  <data key="d7">chunk-f598012485ed9effde140d4a561fd5da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dca5f3a8de43d3e2bc3bc88b3703f62</data>
  <data key="d8">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="TINTAGEL" target="CHOUGH">
  <data key="d5">0.8</data>
  <data key="d6">The relationship between the chough and Tintagel is symbolic and deeply rooted in local folklore. The chough is believed to be the reincarnation of King Arthur's soul, and it is associated with the ruins of Tintagel. This relationship reflects the cultural and spiritual significance of the site and the belief in the continued presence of legendary figures in the natural world.</data>
  <data key="d7">chunk-f598012485ed9effde140d4a561fd5da</data>
  <data key="d8">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="TINTAGEL" target="LOST BELLS">
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
  <data key="d6">The relationship between the lost bells and Tintagel is indirect but significant. The bells were brought to the cove, and their loss is tied to the tragic event that occurred there. Over time, the bells have become a symbol of the mystery and sorrow associated with the site, creating a second-order relationship between the bells and the location.</data>
