<edge source="KING ARTHUR" target="CORNISH CHOUGH">
  <data key="d5">0.6</data>
  <data key="d6">The Cornish chough is indirectly connected to the legend of King Arthur through local superstition, which claims that the mythical figure haunts the coast in the form of the bird. This second-order relationship links the animal to the myth, reinforcing the cultural and symbolic significance of both.</data>
