<edge source="CORNWALL" target="CHARLES">
  <data key="d5">1.5</data>
  <data key="d6">Charles guides the narrator and others through Cornwall, providing directions and recommendations for places to visit. His role is crucial in shaping the experience of the journey, as he ensures that the group sees the most interesting parts of the region.&lt;SEP&gt;The relationship between Charles and the mining community in Cornwall is indirect. Charles explains how the mining business has declined, affecting the community and leading to emigration or starvation. This reflects a second-order relationship between the mining industry and the people of Cornwall.</data>
