<edge source="OLD GENTLEMAN" target="GREEN BANK HOTEL">
  <data key="d5">0.7</data>
  <data key="d6">The travelers choose to stay at the Green Bank Hotel instead of the Falmouth Hotel, influenced by the old gentleman's advice. This is a second-order relationship, as the advice indirectly affects their choice of accommodation. The significance of this relationship lies in how the travelers' preferences are shaped by external input, leading them to prioritize comfort and simplicity over luxury.</data>
