  <data key="d8">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="LIZARD" target="GROUP">
  <data key="d5">1.2999999999999998</data>
  <data key="d6">The group is connected to the Lizard through their stay and interactions with local figures like Esther and John Curgenven. This relationship is indirect and reflects the social and cultural ties of the region. It contributes to the sense of community and belonging in the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;The relationship between the group and the Lizard is one of transformation and emotional growth. Initially, the Lizard was just a place on a map, but it becomes a meaningful location for the group. This relationship is significant because it reflects the group's changing perception of the place. The impact of this relationship is that it deepens the group's connection to the location and enhances their overall experience.</data>
  <data key="d7">chunk-94e0080d8e548382ec3fd09c122e9b19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-000278539400b09a416764f3bc60efe5</data>
