</edge>
<edge source="LIZARD" target="LIZARD STORM">
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
  <data key="d6">The relationship between the Lizard storm and the Lizard location is one of causation and effect. The storm occurs in the Lizard area, and its intensity is attributed to the specific characteristics of the region. The storm's impact on the Lizard is significant, as it disrupts daily life and creates a sense of fear and uncertainty. The relationship is direct, as the storm is a natural phenomenon that affects the location. The storm's occurrence highlights the vulnerability of the Lizard to extreme weather conditions.</data>
  <data key="d7">chunk-cfb65c6e4369170c3277959468b587be</data>
  <data key="d8">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="LIZARD" target="STORM">
  <data key="d5">0.9</data>
  <data key="d6">The storm in the Lizard has a direct impact on the daily activities of the characters, creating challenges such as wet conditions and limiting movement. This relationship highlights the influence of weather on the environment and the lives of the people in the area. The storm is a central factor in the narrative's setting and mood.</data>
  <data key="d7">chunk-9baf49d70e5cdf906cbc1334a05b60e0</data>
  <data key="d8">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="LIZARD" target="STORMS">
  <data key="d5">0.7</data>
  <data key="d6">The Lizard is indirectly connected to the storms and fog through its geographical location. These natural disasters are common in the area, and they contribute to the dangers faced by ships navigating the coast. This relationship highlights the environmental and safety implications of the location.</data>
  <data key="d7">chunk-5d3bdb332242dccc51989976c4f0ce2e</data>
  <data key="d8">2</data>
</edge>
<edge source="LIZARD" target="FOG">
  <data key="d5">0.6</data>
  <data key="d6">The Lizard is also indirectly connected to the fog through its coastal environment. The fog is a recurring challenge that affects navigation and requires the efforts of lifeboat crews and coastguards. This relationship emphasizes the ongoing impact of the natural conditions on the region.</data>
