<edge source="I" target="LIZARD STORM">
  <data key="d5">1.7000000000000002</data>
  <data key="d6">The relationship between the Lizard storm and the narrator's emotional state is one of influence and transformation. The storm causes the narrator to feel a sense of fear and awe, which influences their behavior and decisions. The storm's intensity leads to the narrator's decision to stay indoors and engage in activities like reading and art. The relationship evolves as the storm progresses, with the narrator initially feeling overwhelmed and later reflecting on the experience. The storm's impact on the narrator's mood and actions is significant.&lt;SEP&gt;The relationship between the narrator and the Lizard storm is one of fear and awe. The storm is described as being more terrifying than any other storm the narrator has experienced, and it significantly impacts the narrator's mood and activities. The storm's intensity and unpredictability create a sense of danger and uncertainty. The relationship evolves as the storm progresses, with the narrator initially feeling overwhelmed and later reflecting on the experience. The storm leads to the narrator's decision to stay indoors and engage in activities like reading and art.</data>
  <data key="d7">chunk-cfb65c6e4369170c3277959468b587be</data>
  <data key="d8">1</data>
</edge>
