  <data key="d5">0.7</data>
  <data key="d6">The relationship between the Lizard storm and the literary works mentioned in the text is one of contrast and reflection. The storm serves as a backdrop for the narrator's engagement with literature, which provides a form of escape and comfort. The storm's intensity contrasts with the calm and reflective nature of the literary works. The relationship is indirect, as the storm influences the narrator's choice of reading material and their interpretation of the texts. The storm's presence enhances the thematic elements of the literary works, particularly those related to idealism and the human condition.</data>
