<edge source="MARAZION" target="PENZANCE">
  <data key="d5">0.6</data>
  <data key="d6">The narrator's preference for the inn at Marazion over the grand hotel in Penzance reflects a broader relationship between comfort and fashion. This second-order relationship highlights the contrast between different types of accommodations and the values they represent. The significance of this relationship is that it underscores the importance of personal taste and authenticity in travel experiences. The relationship evolved as the narrator reflected on the differences between the two places, ultimately valuing the simplicity and warmth of the inn over the formality of the hotel. This preference influenced the overall tone of the journey.</data>
